          human: "Mariagenspiel is the historical ancestor of the vast 'Marriage' family of card games, which includes global hits like Sixty-Six, Schnapsen, Pinochle, and Belote. Its name literally means 'Marriage Game', referring to the core mechanic: earning bonus points by holding and declaring a King and Queen of the same suit. It is a trick-taking game where players must balance the pursuit of card points with the opportunistic timing of their marriages.",
